  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the left-sided limit at $x=4$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & \\text{\u00a0for\u00a0}\\,0\\le x<4 \\\\ 2 & \\text{\u00a0for\u00a0}\\,x=4 \\\\ \\sqrt{x-2} & \\text{\u00a0for\u00a0}\\,x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Approaching from the left, we have $x<4,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}\\sqrt{x} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
